</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 30px;">The Nature of Jesus</h1>
  <ul style="list-style-type: square;">
    <li>Grace and truth came through Jesus Christ (John 1:17)
      <ul style="list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 10px;">
        <li>Instead of simply telling us that we were broken, Christ gave us a way to fix what was wrong.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>As we model after Jesus in workplace...
      <ul style="list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 10px;">
        <li>How do we offer grace?
          <ul style="list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 5px;">
            <li>Even when they are performing poorly</li>
            <li>Even when I feel like they are taking advantage</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>How do we speak truth?
          <ul style="list-style-type: circle; margin-top: 5px;">
            <li>About what is happening</li>
            <li>About why we are concerned</li>
            <li>About the importance of them needing to change</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Limitations of an “ or ” approach</li>
  </ul>
  <div style="float: right; margin-top: 100px; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 50%;">
    <div style="text-align: center;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 5px;">AND</h3>
      <h2 style="font-size: 40px; margin-top: 0;">Grace <span style="color: #d93c3c;">OR</span> Truth</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

